1.Objective
Dump the exposed source code and retrieve the flag


2.Reconnaissance
The challenge description suggested that the developer had exposed more than just the website.
The application was accessible on TCP port 8080

3.Enumeration
Performed directory enumeration using ffuf: ffuf -u http://TARGET:8080/FUZZ \-w /usr/share/wordlists/dirb/common.txt, which lead to a .git/HEAD, ref: refs/heads/main which confirm  that the git was publicly accessible

4.Source Code, I found files:
./app.js
./README.md- this one contained the actual flag, that had not been removed bef dep
./index.html


5. Vulnerability
Exposed Git Repository
OWASP
A05 Security Misconfiguration

6.Mitigation
-Never expose the .git directory
-Remove VCS metadata before deployment
-Block access to hidden files
-Review repositories before production deployment
